y-api operating as a managed service throughout a genuine global OOM event while the kernel selected and killed the designated memory hog. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, restart scheduling was acknowledged, its boot ID changed from 96c08b66-5aa4-4e9a-b76f-04e2c6e34ced to b7d1651d-8115-41ef-b514-93021b992dd1, and service, data, OOM protection, listener, and system health recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate that restart.","limitations":["The systemd-reported MemoryPeak for the terminated hog is inconsistent with the kernel's approximately 1.8 GiB RSS record, but the kernel global-OOM and killed-process messages directly establish the required behavior."]}
